    steps: ["Compare small and large transfers under the same path and security context.", "Inspect advertised sizes, encapsulation overhead and applicable path-MTU feedback.", "Look for repeated large sequence ranges without acknowledgments.", "Use bounded authorized probes or deterministic offline cases, not uncontrolled scans.", "Reduce the configured test packet size in an isolated lab and confirm whether delivery changes."],
    example: { given: "Path IP MTU 1400; sender emits 1500-byte IPv4 packets with DF set; required feedback is filtered.", result: "Large packets are dropped and the sender may repeatedly retransmit unless another discovery mechanism adapts.", steps: ["The 1500-byte packet cannot fit 1400.", "DF prohibits IPv4 router fragmentation.", "The router's too-big information does not reach the source in this scenario.", "Small handshake packets still fit, explaining partial success."] },
